# CI lint conformance (actionlint + shellcheck)

These are concrete fixes for real CI failures, kept here so the same class of
failure is caught before push instead of after a run fails.

- **Group sequential summary/file redirects.** Multiple consecutive
  `echo ... >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"` (or any other file) lines trip
  shellcheck SC2129. Write:
  ```bash
  {
    echo "### Title"
    echo ""
    echo "line"
  } >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
  ```
  not one `>>` per line.

- **Guard every segment of a `rm -rf` built from variables.** If a deleted path
  is assembled as `"${A}/${B}"`, an empty/unset `A` or `B` can collapse it to
  `/`. Shellcheck SC2115 catches this. Always write
  `rm -rf "${A:?}/${B:?}"`, not `rm -rf "${A}/${B}"`.

- **Declare every secret a step actually reads, even environment-sourced
  ones.** actionlint type-checks `secrets.NAME` against the workflow's
  `on.workflow_call.secrets:` block. If a job binds `environment: <name>` and
  relies on GitHub's environment-secret exception (the secret is never passed
  by the caller, only exposed because the job is bound to that GitHub
  Environment), you must still declare it in `secrets:` as `required: false`
  with a comment explaining the caller does not map it. See
  `reusable-deploy-gae-node.yml`, `reusable-deploy-firebase-node.yml`, and
  `reusable-run-tests-allure.yml` (`DOPPLER_TOKEN`) for the pattern. Do not
  add a fake `# actionlint-disable-next-line` comment — actionlint has no
  inline suppression directive, so that silently does nothing and the lint
  job keeps failing.

- **actionlint runs against every file matching `.github/workflows/*.yml`.**
  A change to any reusable/called workflow is linted even when no ops
  (`workflow_dispatch`/`schedule`) workflow changed in the same PR. Don't
  assume a "backend-only" or "docs-only" change skips this job.

- **Re-check the whole repo for the same pattern, not just the reported
  line.** When CI reports one instance of SC2129, SC2115, or an undeclared
  secret, grep every workflow and script for the same shape before pushing
  the fix — the next CI run will surface the next instance one failure at a
  time otherwise.
